   "subject": "Reference indicator scaling (marker method): numerical vs categorial",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Hi all,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Question about how lavaan handles the marker method with categorical variables. The literature (Kamata, Bauer) suggests that</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">1) for numerical indicators, the lambda for one the indicators is set to one.  </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">2) for categorical indicators, the lambda for one the indicators is set to one, and the threshold for the same indicator is set to zero. </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">For the code below, it seems that behavior of 1) is implemented although the variables are indicated as ordered. Is this correct?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">My simulations are more stable with the current implementation 1), get unexpected results when setting the threshold to zero in the model... I was wondering why 2) is not implemented... Any reasons?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><div class=\"gmail_default\"><a href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10705510701758406\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10705510701758406&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422753087000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0WHckoBJ4DlplH52yw6UgT\">https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10705510701758406</a>  <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"></div></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">HS9 &lt;- HolzingerSwineford1939[,c(&quot;x1&quot;,&quot;x2&quot;,&quot;x3&quot;,&quot;x4&quot;,&quot;x5&quot;,<br>                                 &quot;x6&quot;,&quot;x7&quot;,&quot;x8&quot;,&quot;x9&quot;)]<br>HSbinary &lt;- as.data.frame( lapply(HS9, cut, 2, labels=FALSE) )<br>HS.model &lt;- &#39; visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3<br>textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6<br>speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 &#39;<br><br>fit &lt;- cfa(HS.model, data=HSbinary, ordered=names(HSbinary),</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422753087000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0_oPJQllERdtcUOGO2tkXj\">std.lv</a>=FALSE, </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">parameterization = &quot;delta&quot;)<br><br>lavInspect(fit, &#39;free&#39;)$lambda<br>lavInspect(fit, &#39;start&#39;)$lambda<br>lavInspect(fit, &#39;est&#39;)$lambda<br><br>lavInspect(fit, &#39;free&#39;)$tau<br>lavInspect(fit, &#39;start&#39;)$tau<br>lavInspect(fit, &#39;est&#39;)$tau<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">  </div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"></div><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/attach/7b6bb54ba259/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"image.png\" width=\"915\" height=\"481\" style=\"margin-right:25px\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"></div><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"></div><div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"></div><br></div><div></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"></div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br><table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size:medium\"><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\" valign=\"middle\" width=\"10\"><p style=\"margin-right:10px;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:14px\"><a href=\"http://www.adaptativa.com.br/\" style=\"text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.adaptativa.com.br/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422753087000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0T-YYDZc1Mx3Wsd2-Y-zHU\"><img src=\"https://ci4.googleusercontent.com/proxy/FE2I4wjFnN2cAFKRmI3TKMszOlSp21wnNu4SqBeCJZBTRvT_FvrlgmwCaxvFTesKdXjysxxb7nvH4if6T_hi884vh3N59BHtgm3-wqx9bgkcnTo-Jw1Bg01c1Tk3qGCKYDUC3lEyIIXfgYCyCshNyEk3Ee8Wg4ibOcS9FfxhtyTI=s0-d-e1-ft#https://htmlsigs.s3.amazonaws.com/logos/files/000/177/391/landscape/adaptativa_256px80pxL_72dpi_SEM_SLOGAN.jpg\" alt=\"Adaptativa\" border=\"0\" height=\"62\" width=\"200\"></a></p></td><td align=\"left\"><p style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:14px;color:rgb(33,33,33)\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;display:inline\">Hugo Harada</span><span style=\"display:inline\"><br></span>Sócio-fundador - COO</font><span style=\"font-size:12px\"></span></p><p style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:14px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;color:rgb(33,33,33);display:inline\">Adaptativa</span> <b>Inteligência Educacional S.A.</b><span style=\"display:inline\"><br></span>Cel: (11) 96345-0390<span style=\"display:inline\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);display:inline\">Rua Claudio Soares, 72 - Sala 411</span><span style=\"display:block\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(33